      "created_at": "2025-09-15T07:14:21.652Z",
      "cooked": "<p>I have a development-related query and need help solving this problem.</p>\n<p>In ERPNext, if I create a custom function to get the item list, I can call this function using Postman like this:</p>\n<p><a href=\"http://127.0.0.1:8009/api/method/custom_app.module.api_file.custom_function\" class=\"onebox\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener nofollow ugc\">http://127.0.0.1:8009/api/method/custom_app.module.api_file.custom_function</a></p>\n<p>But instead of this, I want to call it using a custom route, for example:</p>\n<p><a href=\"http://127.0.0.1:8009/form/items/item_list\" class=\"onebox\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener nofollow ugc\">http://127.0.0.1:8009/form/items/item_list</a></p>\n<p>Is this possible in ERPNext? I tried writing some code in hooks.py to override the route, but it’s not working. How can I achieve this?</p>\n<p>Below are my testing codes:</p>\n<ol>\n<li>\n<p>routes = [<br>\n{“from_route”: “/api/v1/custom_route”, “to_method”: “learn.learn.api.custom_item_list”}<br>\n]</p>\n</li>\n<li>\n<p>override_whitelisted_methods = {<br>\n“/api/v1/custom_route”: “learn.learn.api.custom_item_list”<br>\n}</p>\n</li>\n<li>\n<p>website_route_rules = [<br>\n{“from_route”: “/form/items”, “to_route”: “api/method/learn.config.py.api.custom_item_list”},<br>\n]</p>\n</li>\n<li>\n<p>app_include = {<br>\n“api”: {<br>\n“/api/v1/custom_route”: “learn.learn.api.custom_item_list”<br>\n}<br>\n}</p>\n</li>\n</ol>\n<p>Do you want me to also suggest the correct working solution for your case?</p>",
